{
  "_doc": "Furniture footprints the walkers keep out of (moved here from tools/loadtest/scenarios.json so the load-test bots and the client's wayfinding trail read one file; sim_core::nav::KeepOut). Each is { id, min, max, cell? }: a plan rectangle [x, z] in metres (the footprint itself; the walkers' clearance is added in code), on every surface in plan, or only on layout cell `cell`'s surfaces. Footprints come from the castle kit placements (data/world/castle_kit.json, props.json): the Great Hall's house tables with their benches, the staff table and chairs, the owl lectern, the hourglass plinth and the Dueling Club benches (great_hall only: the Burrowsby common room, the kitchen corridor and the cellars lie below them); the Undercroft Walk's dry well (gf_undercroft only); castle M5b's room furniture that stands in the way (docs/art/castle-kit.md: the Kitchens' long tables, the library's double bookcases and reading tables, the Trophy Room's cases); castle M5c's courtyard and court dressing (castle-kit.md: the fountain, the Exchange Yard's stalls, benches, planters, lamp posts, the gatehouse towers and every free-standing arcade pier; the Owl Exchange court's notice wall, perch tree and crate stacks); the Entrance Hall's Clubs and Societies desk and its chair (clubs_*); the Hospital Wing's beds and screens (hospital_*) and the Clock Tower Courtyard's well, benches, planters, lamp posts and arcade piers (clock_*). A load-test scenario with furniture_keep_out uses those on its cells (all of them when it has no cells); the trail uses all.",
  "version": 1,
